-- ============================================================================
-- Phase 9 · rule-pack outlines — replace the stub packs with real trees
--
-- WHAT THIS CLOSES
-- migrations/20260529_phase9_backfill.sql seeded nda/bla/maa/jnda/denovo as
-- five top-level rows each and said so plainly: "These are stripped-down
-- summaries; the full outlines will be updated in a later kit."  This is that
-- kit.  Until now a biotech org creating its BLA -- the segment's own headline
-- pathway -- was scaffolded a five-node outline by
-- server/services/c2c/scaffold-project-documents.ts, and the Vault tree, the
-- document outline endpoint and the authoring canvas all faithfully rendered
-- those five nodes.  The mechanism worked; it had almost nothing to render.
-- Nothing errored, which is why this survived: a pipeline that succeeds
-- end-to-end while carrying nothing looks exactly like one that works.
--
-- ind:mhra is included for the same reason though it came from a different
-- migration (20260528).  It carried UK Module 1 and no M2-M5 at all, so a UK
-- filer met the same hollow dossier.  Fixing it here rather than granting it a
-- standing exception is what lets the companion contract test assert "no live
-- pack is a stub" with no allow-list -- an allow-list is where the next stub
-- would hide.
--
-- WHY NEW VERSIONS RATHER THAN AN UPDATE
-- c2c_rule_packs is keyed (doc_type, agency, version) and c2c_documents carries
-- a composite FK to it.  Rewriting a pack's required_sections in place would
-- silently change the content of a pack that already-scaffolded documents claim
-- to have been built against -- the audit trail would still say
-- rule_pack_version = 'ich-m4-v2.0' while that pack now meant something else.
-- In a 21 CFR Part 11 table that is not a shortcut, it is a falsified record.
--
-- So: insert the full packs as new versions, then mark the old ones superseded.
-- The scaffolder selects
--     WHERE superseded_by IS NULL ORDER BY effective_from DESC LIMIT 1
-- so new projects pick up the full outline while existing documents keep the
-- version they were actually built from.  Nothing already on disk changes.
--
-- De Novo additionally moves off 'fda-510k-2024'.  A De Novo is a 513(f)(2)
-- classification request, not a 510(k); the stub inherited the 510(k) version
-- string and the two lineages have been sharing an identity that is not real.
--
-- SECTION COUNTS
--   ind:mhra 4 -> 63     bla:fda  5 -> 71     nda:fda    5 -> 71
--   maa:ema  5 -> 73     jnda:pmda 5 -> 64    denovo:fda 5 -> 28
--
-- PROVENANCE OF THE OUTLINES
-- Structural scaffolds derived from the published specifications: ICH M4 for
-- Modules 2-5, FDA eCTD Module 1 (US regional) for NDA/BLA, EU eCTD Module 1
-- (Notice to Applicants Vol 2B) for MAA, the UK regional M1 for MHRA, PMDA eCTD
-- Module 1 for J-NDA, and FDA De Novo content guidance.  A pack defines the
-- outline a filer works against.  It is NOT a determination of what a given
-- application is required to contain -- that follows current agency guidance
-- and the sponsor's own RA review, and the mandatory flags here are defaults to
-- be tuned per programme, not regulatory advice.
--
-- Packs left alone deliberately: mod2, mod3, csr, protocol, ib, psur, briefing,
-- cer, pma, k510.  Several are flat or shallow, but a flat outline is correct
-- for a single-purpose document -- Module 2's summaries and a CER's A0-A8 have
-- no hierarchy to express.  Shallow is not the same defect as hollow.
--
-- Idempotent: ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING on the insert, and each supersede UPDATE is
-- guarded on superseded_by IS NULL.
-- ============================================================================

BEGIN;

-- Guarded so this file is safe in the durable apply-set (scripts/db/migration-set.mjs),
-- which runs against databases that may not have had the Phase 9 schema applied.
-- Same bare-CI-safe DO-block pattern as 20260529_phase9_backfill.sql.
DO $mig$
BEGIN
  IF to_regclass('public.c2c_rule_packs') IS NULL THEN
    RAISE NOTICE 'c2c_rule_packs not present - skipping rule-pack outlines (Phase 9 schema not applied here)';
    RETURN;
  END IF;

  -- 1. The full packs, as new versions.
